00:11:27,745 --> 00:11:31,230
from the register step,

291
00:11:31,230 --> 00:11:34,460
and the number of devices
that are associated with it.

292
00:11:34,460 --> 00:11:35,930
You cdev del,

293
00:11:35,930 --> 00:11:37,790
when you're ready to delete

294
00:11:37,790 --> 00:11:40,440
the device when there's
no more accesses.

295
00:11:40,440 --> 00:11:42,445
For example,

296
00:11:42,445 --> 00:11:45,055
the scull device driver
that we talked about,

297
00:11:45,055 --> 00:11:47,110
there's a char device
structure that's

298
00:11:47,110 --> 00:11:49,330
embedded inside the
scull device structure.

299
00:11:49,330 --> 00:11:51,860
This is a pretty
common way to do it.

300
00:11:55,020 --> 00:11:57,910
For instance, when
you open the device

301
00:11:57,910 --> 00:12:00,190
node from User space that will

302
00:12:00,190 --> 00:12:02,440
ultimately map to this
open function pointer

303
00:12:02,440 --> 00:12:05,335
that you'll implement and
set up in your f_ops table.

304
00:12:05,335 --> 00:12:07,900
The common things that
you do an open method,

305
00:12:07,900 --> 00:12:09,415
you check for device error.

306
00:12:09,415 --> 00:12:11,020
If there's some reason
that you shouldn't

307
00:12:11,020 --> 00:12:12,940
allow operations to happen on

308
00:12:12,940 --> 00:12:14,830
your device you
check for that here

309
00:12:14,830 --> 00:12:17,215
and you return the
appropriate error.

310
00:12:17,215 --> 00:12:19,630
If it was the first open
that was happening,

311
00:12:19,630 --> 00:12:22,420
you might want to do some
initialization on the device.

312
00:12:22,420 --> 00:12:25,240
You would update
the f_ops pointer

313
00:12:25,240 --> 00:12:28,600
to point to file operations.

314
00:12:28,600 --> 00:12:32,320
Then if needed you
could allocate and

315
00:12:32,320 --> 00:12:35,800
fill the private data
member of the file pointer.

316
00:12:35,800 --> 00:12:38,710
Here's what the function
prototype looks like.

317
00:12:38,710 --> 00:12:42,475
It's passing in an inode its
structure and struct file.

318
00:12:42,475 --> 00:12:44,230
One thing that's
notably missing from

319
00:12:44,230 --> 00:12:46,360
that prototype is
the c_dev structure,

