00:13:44,890 --> 00:13:46,615
to my scull_dev structure?

346
00:13:46,615 --> 00:13:48,805
It turns out there's
a pretty cool tool

347
00:13:48,805 --> 00:13:52,015
that you can use for
this that's based of

348
00:13:52,015 --> 00:13:55,330
the fact that you can
do pointer math in c to

349
00:13:55,330 --> 00:13:56,800
figure out where a structure

350
00:13:56,800 --> 00:13:58,885
is based on the
structure definition.

351
00:13:58,885 --> 00:14:01,120
This container of macro is

352
00:14:01,120 --> 00:14:03,400
going to take a
pointer and a type,

353
00:14:03,400 --> 00:14:05,079
in this case, the structure,

354
00:14:05,079 --> 00:14:06,730
and then a field
within this structure,

355
00:14:06,730 --> 00:14:08,140
so the c_dev field.

356
00:14:08,140 --> 00:14:10,630
If I have a pointer
to this element,

357
00:14:10,630 --> 00:14:12,100
and I know that this
element is that

358
00:14:12,100 --> 00:14:14,230
this specific location
in the structure,

359
00:14:14,230 --> 00:14:18,675
the container of macro can
do the math to figure out,

360
00:14:18,675 --> 00:14:20,670
okay, where's the first byte of

361
00:14:20,670 --> 00:14:23,310
this structure based
