you at process exit.

419
00:16:43,405 --> 00:16:45,550
When the process exits,

420
00:16:45,550 --> 00:16:47,680
you're going to be
guaranteed to get

421
00:16:47,680 --> 00:16:50,020
exactly one release per open.

422
00:16:50,020 --> 00:16:54,159
Multiple processes might close

423
00:16:54,159 --> 00:16:57,805
if a fork or a doop
happen for instance.

424
00:16:57,805 --> 00:17:00,380
Like what we used for
creating daemons.

425
00:17:00,380 --> 00:17:03,600
Multiple process might close,

426
00:17:03,600 --> 00:17:06,420
but only the last clause is
going to result in a release.

427
00:17:06,420 --> 00:17:09,060
All this is handled for you
by the Kernel framework

428
00:17:09,060 --> 00:17:10,680
and you're going to be
guaranteed that you

429
00:17:10,680 --> 00:17:13,330
get exactly one release open.